# Swing: a medium swing at ~124, eighths swung as triplets (the and of a beat at tick 320). Drums from the
# Groove MIDI Dataset (drummer 10, a jazz swing at 124, CC BY 4.0: styles/README.md); the rest written for
# Polly over C M7, in 3rd-5th-7th voicings so it follows sevenths, sixths and half-diminished alike.
# Main A: time on the closed hi-hat (the drummer's open-hat chick played closed), a walking bass in quarters, piano comping the Charleston, a soft organ.
# Main B: the drummer on the ride, the walk with triplet pickups, busier piano, a vibraphone line, the
# organ up.
style Swing
tempo 124

track d1 type=bypass chan=10 vol=110 rev=40
track d2 type=bypass chan=10 vol=110 rev=40   # shares channel 10 with d1: the same mixer
track pc type=bypass chan=10 vol=110 rev=40
track ba type=bass program=32 chan=2 lo=E1 hi=G3 hikey=F# vol=122 rev=24
track c1 type=chord1 program=0 chan=3 lo=Bb3 hi=E5 hikey=F# vol=100 pan=48 rev=48
track c2 type=chord1 program=11 chan=4 lo=E4 hi=E6 hikey=F# vol=80 pan=84 rev=56
track c3 type=chord2 program=16 chan=5 lo=G3 hi=C5 vol=48 pan=64 rev=50 cho=30

[main a]
bars 2
beats 4
track d1
drums from=drums/drummer10-session1-1_jazz-swing_124_beat_4-4.mid start=9 bars=2 map=ohh:chh scale=kick:70,snare:55,chh:80
track ba
# walking: root, a step, the 3rd, the 5th; then root, 5th below, the 6th and the 7th up into the next root
1.1.0  C2 440 104
1.2.0  D2 440 86
